psx_sdram_ctrl.sv is copied unchanged from github.com/GuardianSoul/openfpga-PlayStation (rtl/memory/psx_sdram_ctrl.sv),
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 PSX Pocket contributors. It is a drop-in for MiSTer's sdram.sv ports and
is simulated there against a strict SDR chip model (sim/memory/tb_psx_sdram_ctrl.sv).

psx_vram_psram.sv is copied unchanged from the same repository (rtl/memory/psx_vram_psram.sv), SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT,
Copyright (c) 2026 PSX Pocket contributors. It implements the MiSTer PSX core's DDR3 port (GPU VRAM) on the Pocket's two CellularRAM chips;
the System 11 GPU is the PSX_MiSTer GPU and speaks the same DDRAM_* protocol.

